# Brief
The brief for this project was to build a full CRUD web application using the MEN stack.
The app needed to support user authentication, data ownership, and complete CRUD functionality while following RESTful routing conventions and demonstrating thoughtful UX decisions.


# Planning
I began the project by clearly defining the problem space and the core MVP features before writing any code.

Planning steps included:
* Writing user stories
* Wireframing basic page layouts for:
	Dashboard
	Subscription list
	Subscription detail view
* Building ERD 
	Defining the data model and relationships (User → Subscriptions)
	Planning CRUD routes and user flows
	Identifying the MVP scope and intentionally cutting “nice-to-have” features

Because this was a solo project, I owned all planning, design, and development decisions.

