# Build Process
The project was built incrementally, starting with authentication and data models, followed by CRUD functionality and finally the dashboard logic.

# Key highlights:
Full CRUD Subscription Management
    Users can:
	    Create subscriptions
	    View all subscriptions
	    Edit subscription details
	    Delete subscriptions

Each subscription is owned by a user and protected via session-based authentication.

Auto Renewal Date Logic
    One feature I’m particularly proud of is the automatic next renewal calculation.
    If a user enters a renewal date that has already passed, the app computes the next valid renewal date based on the subscription type (weekly, monthly, yearly).

This logic is used consistently across:
    Dashboard upcoming renewals
	Subscription list sorting
	Individual subscription detail pages

Dashboard Insights
    The dashboard aggregates meaningful information:
	    Active, paused, and cancelled subscription counts
	    Estimated monthly spend (normalized across weekly/monthly/yearly plans)
	    Upcoming renewals within the next 30 days


# Challenges
* Renewal date logic:
    Handling past dates, different billing cycles, and trial subscriptions required careful date manipulation and edge case handling.
* Data consistency across views:
    Ensuring the same renewal logic applied correctly on the dashboard, index page, and show page took iteration and refactoring.
* Scope control:
    It was tempting to add advanced features early, but staying focused on a solid MVP was the biggest challenge.

# Wins
* Successfully implemented a reliable auto-renewal date system
* Clean separation between logic (routes) and presentation (EJS views)
* Consistent UI and interaction patterns across the app
* Completed a fully functional MEN stack app independently


# Key Learnings / Takeaways
* Gained strong confidence working with:
* Express routing
* MongoDB + Mongoose
* Session-based authentication
* Learned how small backend decisions directly affect UX
* Developed a deeper appreciation for the complexity behind “simple” features


# Future Improvements
* Add categories or tags for subscriptions
* Introduce renewal reminders or notifications
* Provide deeper insights into spending habits
* Improve accessibility and keyboard navigation
* Add support for multiple currencies with conversion
